  "id": "filamentstreetlaunderette",
  "neon": "#9fffd0",
  "note": "FILAMENT STREET LAUNDERETTE — the launderette on Filament Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: a shopfront lit like an operating theatre and steamed up from the inside, so the\nlight comes out soft and green; the name spelled out across the fascia in individual letters, one\nof which has been replaced with a slightly different font and is now what everyone looks at; warm\nair pushing out under the door.\n\nSo the front is a wide steamed shop window over a tiled stall riser, the door at one end, white\nglazed tile everywhere, and the name as eleven separate letters on the fascia, each its own board.\nThe R is in a different hand. Dryer vents line the flank and stain the tile under them.",
